<title>FRANCE: ADP export traffic up 7.7pct in December 1996.</title>
<headline>ADP export traffic up 7.7pct in December 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>December 1996 export traffic from the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 50,786 tonnes, up 7.7 percent on the same month in 1995, Aeroports de Paris, (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>The ADP's global export traffic in December 1996, by region, with percentage change on December 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p> Domestic		 3,669 tonnes   up   12.6pct</p>
<p> European Union	 5,860 tonnes   up   27.1</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	  1,254 tonnes   up   28.1</p>
<p> North Africa	     903 tonnes   down 10.2</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa   4,629 tonnes   up    6.7</p>
<p> North America	 13,723 tonnes   up   14.7</p>
<p> French territories   3,182 tonnes   up   10.3</p>
<p> Latin America	  2,630 tonnes   down  8.4</p>
<p> Middle East	    4,762 tonnes   up    7.5</p>
<p> Far East		10,174 tonnes   down  5.8</p>
<p> Total		   50,786 tonnes   up    7.7</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
